        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 85-year-old female admitted on 31/03/1985 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination confirmed widespread expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gases revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She has been discharged home with oral prednisolone taper and inhaler optimisation. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Should you have any concerns, do not hesitate to contact me.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
